{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun2/packet-a.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin first shipments — the step that brings revenue — before the end of calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Vera Rubin reaches first shipments (start of revenue) by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"period\": \"End of calendar 2026, the date the item supports ('could begin shipping later this year' relative to its 2 July 2026 date).\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA quarterly earnings releases and 10-Q/10-K disclosures confirming Vera Rubin first shipments/revenue, and shipping confirmations.\",\n   \"why_a_separate_bet\": \"Vera Rubin first shipments are a manufacturing/ramp milestone settled by NVIDIA's own delivery and revenue disclosures; the credit-support theses (clean-1, clean-2) track the dollar amount of guarantees/backstops NVIDIA extends to cloud partners. NVIDIA could ship Vera Rubin on schedule while extending little credit support, or delay shipments while guaranteeing partners' capacity, so the two answers move independently.\"\n  },\n  \"thesis_id\": \"u1 clean-3\",\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-02\",\n   \"publisher\": \"fool.com\",\n   \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n   \"text\": \"Microsoft ( MSFT +1.28% ) and Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) are two heavyweights in the technology world and key players in artificial intelligence (AI). Microsoft seems to have its hand in every tech market segment, especially anything involving enterprise customers. Meanwhile, Nvidia has become the de facto leader in GPU chips used in AI data centers.\\nBoth stocks have made investors very wealthy over the years. But which of these top AI stocks is the better buy for the next three years? This article will explain why I like Microsoft a tad more. Although, as you'll see below, it's hard to go wrong with either one.\\nVera Rubin likely means Nvidia has more growth ahead\\nNvidia has enjoyed one of the most impressive growth spurts in history over these past few years as the AI build-out juiced demand for its GPUs. This supercycle continues to rage on. Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year. CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\nWall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year. Nvidia's valuation is already well below its high at less than 19 times sales, and it might become much cheaper as these next 24 months play out.\\nMicrosoft is pivoting to capitalize on its enterprise customer base\\nMicrosoft originally tied its AI hopes to OpenAI. Although Microsoft has done well with its OpenAI investment and enjoyed significant cloud computing growth as a result of the partnership, it has still struggled to establish itself as a key AI player. Users, especially enterprises, have opted for Anthropic's Claude among other AI models. As a result, Microsoft shifted to a multi-model strategy and has reportedly considered adding open-source models to Copilot Cowork to lower token costs.\\nInvestors should applaud Microsoft's willingness to adapt. The company has deeply entrenched relationships with the enterprise world, which gives Microsoft more margin for error in fine-tuning its AI strategy than most companies. Plus, Microsoft's Azure remains a formidable growth engine, with a staggering $627 billion in remaining commercial performance obligations.\\nNvidia's data center business has grown so much that the stock has become a concentrated investment in this ongoing supercycle. That means Nvidia has a sky-high ceiling with Vera Rubin shipping soon, but it's riskier in that the floor is much lower if companies stop pouring all this money into AI infrastructure. Meanwhile, Microsoft remains highly diversified across software, cloud computing, and AI. That lowers the company's ceiling, but it's also the safer stock.\\nMicrosoft's impressive track record typically earns it a premium valuation. The stock has traded at an average of almost 33 times its trailing-12-month earnings over the past decade, but trades at just 22 times its earnings today. Meanwhile, Wall Street analysts expect the company to grow earnings by 16% to 17% annually over the next three to five years.\\nWhile some may opt for Nvidia's immense growth potential , Microsoft rarely offers a valuation compelling enough to buy into.\\nJustin Pope is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering information technology, consumer discretionary, consumer staples, and industrials. Prior to The Motley Fool, Justin was a business manager for an industrial company.\\nBy Justin Pope – Jul 2, 2026 at 12:43PM EST\"\n  },\n  \"ladders\": [\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-1\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform have begun first shipments by 2026-12-31?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Yes\",\n       \"condition\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin are confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"No\",\n       \"condition\": \"No first shipment of Vera Rubin is confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-2\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"Will Vera Rubin start shipping to customers before the end of calendar 2026?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Yes\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA confirms Vera Rubin shipments to customers began in calendar 2026.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"No\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not confirmed that Vera Rubin shipments to customers began in calendar 2026.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-3\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"no_ladder\": \"Nothing in the topic can be checked on a date.\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-4\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform have begun first shipments by 2026-12-31?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Yes\",\n       \"condition\": \"No first shipment of Vera Rubin is confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"No\",\n       \"condition\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin are confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-5\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform have begun first shipments by 2026-09-30?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2026-09-30\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Yes\",\n       \"condition\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin are confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-09-30.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"No\",\n       \"condition\": \"No first shipment of Vera Rubin is confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-09-30.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-3-6\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform have begun first shipments by 2026-12-31?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Yes\",\n       \"condition\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin are confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"No\",\n       \"condition\": \"No first shipment of Vera Rubin is confirmed to have taken place on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will the outstanding amount of NVIDIA's supply (purchase) commitments to suppliers be at its next annual report — the obligations that lock it into buying capacity and services for its AI systems?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The outstanding supply/purchase commitments disclosed in NVIDIA's next annual report, compared with the $119 billion cited in this item.\",\n   \"period\": \"Next annual report (Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, likely filed early 2027); set by the reason — an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"binding_obligation\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's annual report on Form 10-K, purchase commitments / commitments and contingencies note, for the fiscal year ending late January 2027.\",\n   \"why_a_separate_bet\": \"clean-1 tracks credit support NVIDIA extends to AI cloud partners (its exposure if they fail to pay); this thesis tracks NVIDIA's own commitments to pay suppliers, the cash it must fund if AI demand disappoints. The two can move in opposite directions and are disclosed in different notes, so an analyst would bet on them separately.\"\n  },\n  \"thesis_id\": \"u1 clean-7\",\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-06\",\n   \"publisher\": \"247wallst.com\",\n   \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n   \"text\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\\nNVIDIA’s fundamentals have never looked stronger, yet its stock is limping through 2026. NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA | NVDA Price Prediction) is up just 3.2% year to date, a striking laggard in a sector where money is flooding into almost everything else.…\\nBy Danielle Liverance\\nNVDA is up just 7% year to date despite 85% revenue growth to $82B, punished for being priced as the consensus AI trade.\\nAMD surged 171% and Micron 305% year to date, rewarding investors who bet on chips with room to reprice rather than perfection already baked in.\\nNvidia's $119B in supply commitments hinge on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools, which is a question the market appears to already be pricing in.\\nNVIDIA’s fundamentals have never looked stronger, yet its stock is limping through 2026. NVIDIA ( NASDAQ:NVDA | NVDA Price Prediction ) is up just 3.2% year to date, a striking laggard in a sector where money is flooding into almost everything else. That is the paradox: the company at the center of the AI buildout has become the black sheep of the chip rally.\\nAdvanced Micro Devices ( NASDAQ:AMD ) has ripped 171.25% year to date. Micron Technology ( NASDAQ:MU ) is up a stunning 304.62%. Intel ( NASDAQ:INTC ), still deep in a turnaround under Lip-Bu Tan, has surged 278.4% on DCAI momentum and NVIDIA’s own $5 billion equity investment. Broadcom ( NASDAQ:AVGO ), the custom-silicon story, is one example of another megacap stock that largely matches NVIDIA’s returns.\\nBut the broader story is one of semiconductor stocks rallying. The VanEck Semiconductor ETF (Nasdaq: SMH) is up 59% year-to-date. The divergence looks set to continue today. The VanEck is up 3% premarket while NVIDIA shares are up just .3%, as of 8:40 a.m. ET. NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\\nThe earnings do not explain the tape. Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion, with data center up 92% to $75.2 billion. CEO Jensen Huang framed it plainly: “Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.” But NVDA trades at a forward P/E of less than 20 now, and when a name becomes the consensus AI trade, even a blowout can underwhelm a market that had already priced perfection. Polymarket sentiment tracks this: end-of-July close-above-$200 probability sits at just 43%.\\nThe narrative is fragmenting. NVIDIA still owns roughly 81% of the AI chip market , but Broadcom’s custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta are eating the story, with Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators. Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year. AMD’s Meta Instinct GPU deal anchors a multi-year hyperscaler thesis , and Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\\nOne important number to watch is the relative size of AMD compared to NVIDIA. Right now, AMD is worth about 18% of NVIDIA’s value. At the beginning of the year, AMD was worth less than 10% NVIDIA. Investors are still piling into companies benefiting from the data center buildout, they’re just not piling into NVIDIA.\\nMicron is a different animal. Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron have avoided the aggressive oversupply that crushed memory pricing in prior cycles, a meaningful break from history. Q3 revenue exploded 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion, and CEO Sanjay Mehrotra pointed to multi-year Strategic Customer Agreements designed to lock in durability. NVIDIA has been smart about locking in its own memory supply as other companies like Apple (Nasdaq: AAPL) have been caught flat footed. And yet, the combined value of Micron, SK Hynix, and Samsung now rivals NVIDIA itself.\\nMost strikingly, Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter, above the peak gross margins NVIDIA ever achieved. Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027. Simply put, the rise of memory is shifting the center of gravity in the data center trade away from NVIDIA and towards memory names.\\nWhich brings the market to the quiet question underneath all of it. Demand looks strong in 2027, but with hyperscalers now having to move into debt and equity offerings, the question of whether growth slows dramatically in 2028 is now front and center on investors minds. The ‘good’ news for NVIDIA investors is the company now trades for just 12X its forecasted 2028 earnings. If a slowdown does come, it’ll likely hit NVIDIA a lot less than names trading for 50X their forecasted 2028 profits.\\nI've spent more than 15 years inside enterprise software, working alongside the finance, sales operations, and HR leaders who run the revenue engines at some of the largest tech companies in the country.\\nMy day job is helping enterprise executives make smarter decisions about retention, compensation, and growth. These are the same operational levers that show up in every earnings report investors actually read. That perspective shapes my writing for 24/7 Wall St.\\nThe headline numbers are easy. The interesting stuff is underneath: how companies make money, what executives are worried about, and what any of it means for the person checking their 401(k) on a Sunday afternoon. I write about personal finance and business as someone who has spent her career inside the rooms where these decisions get made.\\nSK Hynix surged 14% Tuesday without a single company-specific headline, and the real test comes July 29 when its earnings either confirm or shatter the bullish memory narrative Micron just set.\"\n  },\n  \"ladders\": [\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-1\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 80,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 80,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 140,000,000,000 USD to below 180,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"180,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-2\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 80,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 80,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 80,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 80,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 140,000,000,000 USD to below 180,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 140,000,000,000 USD to below 180,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"180,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"180,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-3\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 80,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 80,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 140,000,000,000 USD to below 180,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"180,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-4\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA reports commitments below $80 billion.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA reports commitments of at least $80 billion and below $110 billion.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA reports commitments of at least $110 billion and below $140 billion.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA reports commitments of at least $140 billion and below $180 billion.\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"NVIDIA reports commitments of at least $180 billion.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-5\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 1,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,000,000,000 USD to below 2,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 2,000,000,000 USD to below 5,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 5,000,000,000 USD to below 10,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"10,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-7-6\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"NVDA\",\n     \"kind\": \"asset\",\n     \"question\": \"What amount of supply and purchase commitments will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n     \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 80,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 80,000,000,000 USD to below 110,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 110,000,000,000 USD to below 140,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 140,000,000,000 USD to below 180,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n       \"condition\": \"180,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will the combined data center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027, the aggregate AI-infrastructure spend Nvidia projects and on which its GPU demand depends?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditure for calendar 2027, as disclosed in their full-year results.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the item's 'next year' from its 2026 date), when the four hyperscalers report full-year capex; set by the item, which projects the figure could reach $1 trillion in 2027 up from around $650 billion in 2026.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"shared_quantity\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The four leading AI hyperscalers' quarterly and full-year capital expenditure disclosures in their earnings releases and 10-K/10-Q filings for FY2027, aggregated.\",\n   \"why_a_separate_bet\": \"clean-3 tracks whether Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform reaches first shipments by end-2026, a product-timing question; this thesis tracks the industry-level capex quantity that drives total GPU demand. They can move independently: Rubin could ship on schedule while hyperscaler capex is cut back, or Rubin could slip while aggregate capex stays high on spending for existing platforms.\"\n  },\n  \"thesis_id\": \"u1 clean-4\",\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-04\",\n   \"publisher\": \"fool.com\",\n   \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n   \"text\": \"Nvidia (NASDAQ: NVDA) investors have had it good for several years. In 2023, 2024, and 2025, it produced market-crushing returns, making it one of the best stocks to own during each of those years. However, 2026 hasn't been that way. The stock is up 5% so far in 2026, which isn't nothing, but compared to the returns that Nvidia investors have enjoyed in recent years, it feels like an absolute failure. On another note, its market-crushing status is in jeopardy for 2026, as the S&P 500 is up nearly 10% for the year.\\nWith Nvidia stock looking like a dud this year, many investors are wondering whether now is the time to cash out and look for other investment opportunities, or to load up on Nvidia shares. Let's take a look, as not everything is as it appears with Nvidia.\\nNvidia was the top AI stock to own over the past three years, due to its market position. Nvidia designs graphics processing units (GPUs) and the hardware that supports them. Although it doesn't own any of the fabrication process itself, it works with several companies that manufacture its GPUs, which it then sells to a wide range of customers.\\nBefore 2023, Nvidia's business was more balanced. However, the massive demand for AI data centers has driven this lineup of GPUs into high demand, and Nvidia's product line has become the go-to for several AI hyperscalers and cloud providers. Nvidia has a complete ecosystem of products that gives its clients everything they need to run an Nvidia-powered data center, locking in clients once they've chosen to use its products.\\nThis bodes well for the future, as AI hyperscalers are spending a massive amount of money this year and beyond to continue building out their AI computing footprints. The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year. Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion. That means more growth is coming to Nvidia, and the investing story is far from complete. Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\nHowever, the stock price doesn't reflect that.\\nNvidia trades at 21.7 times forward earnings, essentially the same price tag as the S&P 500. This conveys that the market believes Nvidia will be a market-average stock after 2026's growth is accounted for. However, Wall Street analysts don't believe that, as they're guiding for major growth next year. That's why the stock looks so cheap when next year's earnings are used to value the stock.\\nAs a result, I think Nvidia is an excellent stock to buy now. None of next year's growth has been priced in, which could lead to strong returns toward the end of this year.\"\n  },\n  \"ladders\": [\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-1\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 450,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 450,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 450,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 450,000,000,000 USD to below 600,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 600,000,000,000 USD to below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 850,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 850,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"850,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"850,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-2\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\\")\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-3\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\\")\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-4\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-5\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2026\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\\")\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\",\n       \"condition\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"ladder\": \"clean-4-6\",\n    \"as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n     \"object\": \"ai-capex\",\n     \"kind\": \"theme\",\n     \"question\": \"What will the combined data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027?\",\n     \"year\": \"2027\",\n     \"due_day\": \"2028-02-15\",\n     \"rungs\": [\n      {\n       \"position\": 1,\n       \"label\": \"Lowest\",\n       \"condition\": \"below 700,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 2,\n       \"label\": \"Low\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 700,000,000,000 USD to below 900,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 3,\n       \"label\": \"Middle\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 900,000,000,000 USD to below 1,100,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 4,\n       \"label\": \"High\",\n       \"condition\": \"from 1,100,000,000,000 USD to below 1,300,000,000,000 USD\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"position\": 5,\n       \"label\": \"Highest\",\n       \"condition\": \"1,300,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-1\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-2\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"The conditions require NVIDIA's confirmation and exclude other shipping confirmations named by the thesis.\",\"why\":\"No marked faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-3\",\"Q\":\"n/a\",\"O\":\"n/a\",\"R\":\"n/a\",\"D\":\"n/a\",\"X\":\"n/a\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"fails\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"First shipments can be checked against the end of 2026.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-4\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"fails\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"Yes says no first shipment was confirmed, while No says first shipments were confirmed.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-5\",\"Q\":\"fails\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"fails\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"September 30 asks about an earlier deadline than the thesis's end of 2026, and neither the thesis nor the article supports that assessment date.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-3\",\"ladder\":\"clean-3-6\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-1\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"fails\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The ladder calls commitments of $180 billion or more strongly bullish, although the thesis concerns the greater obligation and funding exposure.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-2\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"fails\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"NVIDIA's own purchase commitments belong to NVDA as an asset, not the ai-capex theme.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-3\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-4\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-5\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"fails\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"A top range beginning at $10 billion is not a fair division around the article's $119 billion in commitments.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-7\",\"ladder\":\"clean-7-6\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-1\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"fails\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"fails\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The middle range of $600–700 billion centers on the prior year's $650 billion rather than NVIDIA's projection that 2027 spending could reach $1 trillion.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-2\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-3\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"fails\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The year field says 2026 while the question asks for calendar 2027.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-4\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-5\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"fails\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The year field says 2026 while the question asks for calendar 2027.\"}\n{\"thesis_id\":\"u1 clean-4\",\"ladder\":\"clean-4-6\",\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No faults identified.\"}"}}
